From: C2000MAX maintainers <noreply@example.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 05:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] net: mediatek: expose HQoS debugfs controls as writable

The vendor debugfs nodes implement write callbacks but several are created
with read-only inode modes.  Besides being misleading, this makes userspace
W_OK probes fail on restricted root environments and prevents EQoS from
publishing an active backend.

Keep the HNAT flow-table control root-only and mark it writable.  QDMA
scheduler and queue nodes are made writable in the patch which introduces
those debugfs files.
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat_debugfs.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat_debugfs.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat_debugfs.c
@@ -5065,4 +5065,4 @@ int hnat_init_debugfs(struct mtk_hnat *h
-	debugfs_create_file("hnat_entry", 0444, root, h,
+	debugfs_create_file("hnat_entry", 0600, root, h,
 			    &hnat_entry_fops);
 	debugfs_create_file("hnat_stats", 0444, root, h,
 			    &hnat_stats_fops);
